{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_7f8399bd-573f-48c4-a404-16275140e4d8","role":"user","created":1775377343,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"call_ab4f38db977ab2e1","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2012_06.txt:The 2-year notes of Series AT-2013 were dated December 31 and issued January 3. They are due December 31, 2013, with interest payable on June 30 and December 31 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-1/8 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\n/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2013_06.txt:The Consolidated Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1985 (Public Law 99-272), enacted April 7, 1986, provided for an increase in the coal tax rates effective April 1, 1986, through December 31, 1995, and a 5-year forgiveness of interest retroactive to October 1, 1985. The 5-year moratorium on interest payments ended on September 30, 1990. Payment of interest on advances resumed in fiscal year 1991. The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1987 (Public Law 100-203, title X, section 10503), signed December 22, 1987, extended the temporary increase in the coal tax through December 31, 2013.","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2012_06.txt:The 2-year notes of Series AT-2013 were dated December 31 and issued January 3. They are due December 31, 2013, with interest payable on June 30 and December 31 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-1/8 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\n/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2013_06.txt:The Consolidated Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1985 (Public Law 99-272), enacted April 7, 1986, provided for an increase in the coal tax rates effective April 1, 1986, through December 31, 1995, and a 5-year forgiveness of interest retroactive to October 1, 1985. The 5-year moratorium on interest payments ended on September 30, 1990. Payment of interest on advances resumed in fiscal year 1991. The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1987 (Public Law 100-203, title X, section 10503), signed December 22, 1987, extended the temporary increase in the coal tax through December 31, 2013.","stderr":"","exit_code":0},"isError":false}}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
