{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775377544-eaUyv8hTGTBtHouxuAWG","role":"assistant","created":1775377557,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The task requires finding ESF assets for December 31, 2013. The problem statement says I need to use \"an official U.S. Treasury or federal government source\" - and from the available resources it seems the June 2014 Treasury Bulletin would normally have this data but it's not provided in the resources folder.\n\nWait, let me re-read the problem. It says:\n\"using an official U.S. Treasury or federal government source, obtain the total ESF assets at December 31, 2013\"\n\nSo this suggests I might need to look up data from an external source, not necessarily from the provided files. But in this evaluation environment without network access, perhaps I should try another approach.\n\nActually, wait - let me look at the problem again. It says the ESF data is available for 2010, 2011, 2012 and the task wants me to compute 2013 from an external source. The task is designed to allow looking up data from an \"official source.\" \n\nHowever, looking at the test setup - it seems like this is a self-contained test and 2013 data should either be in the available resources or there's a way to find it. Let me check if there's any 2014 bulletin or other source.\n\nActually, I wonder if the issue is that December 31, 2013 is covered in a different Treasury Bulletin (June 2014). Let me check if there's a treasury_bulletin_2014 file or check what's the convention. Let me also search online more carefully.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_15d8ba815b67db10","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Try fetching data using Treasury's data API\nimport urllib.request\nimport json\nimport ssl\n\n# Treasury financial statements are available\nurls = [\n    \"https://www.fiscal.treasury.gov/files/reports-statements/tesf/tesf-fy2013.pdf\",\n    \"https://www.fiscal.treasury.gov/files/reports-statements/tesf/tesf-2013.pdf\",\n]\n\nfor url in urls:\n    try:\n        context = ssl.create_default_context()\n        context.check_hostname = False\n        context.verify_mode = ssl.CERT_NONE\n        req = urllib.request.Request(url)\n        response = urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=10, context=context)\n        print(f\"Success: {url}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Failed {url}: {type(e).__name__}\")\n        \n# Also try the status page which should have summary data\ntry:\n    url = \"https://www.fiscal.treasury.gov/reports-statements/tesf/status.html\"\n    context = ssl.create_default_context()\n    context.check_hostname = False\n    context.verify_mode = ssl.CERT_NONE\n    req = urllib.request.Request(url)\n    response = urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15, context=context)\n    content = response.read().decode('utf-8')\n    # Look for 2013 data\n    if '2013' in content:\n        print(\"Found 2013 data in status page!\")\n        import re\n        matches = re.findall(r'2013.*?\\\\$[^\\\\n]+', content)\n        for m in matches[:5]:\n            print(m)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Status page error: {e}\")\n    \nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
